From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] iOS: send the PGN 126996 request at most once a minute

While no TX-capable gateway is identified, PrepareForTX sends a broadcast
request for PGN 126996 (product information) before every transmit. Every
device on the bus answers it; through a gateway that is not recognised
(m_TX_available never becomes true) this flooded the NMEA 2000 bus. Limit
the request to once a minute.

Inside #ifdef __OCPN__IOS__ for now. The same problem exists on all
platforms (OpenCPN/OpenCPN#5537); a general fix is proposed separately.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 model/src/comm_drv_n2k_net.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/model/src/comm_drv_n2k_net.cpp b/model/src/comm_drv_n2k_net.cpp
index 9af2961b8..8eca73ca6 100644
--- a/model/src/comm_drv_n2k_net.cpp
+++ b/model/src/comm_drv_n2k_net.cpp
@@ -1906,6 +1906,16 @@ bool CommDriverN2KNet::PrepareForTX() {
   if (m_TX_available)
     return true;
   else {
+#ifdef __OCPN__IOS__
+    // iOS: this request goes to all devices on the bus, each answering with
+    // product information. Upstream sent it on every transmit; with a YDNR (no
+    // "YDEN") m_TX_available never becomes true and the bus got flooded. At
+    // most once per minute.
+    static wxLongLong s_last_probe = 0;
+    wxLongLong now = wxGetUTCTimeMillis();
+    if (s_last_probe != 0 && now - s_last_probe < 60000) return false;
+    s_last_probe = now;
+#endif
     // Send a broadcast request for PGN 126996, Product Information
     std::vector<unsigned char> payload;
     payload.push_back(0x14);
